hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28013","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Abi Al-Abbas and Yunus ibn Muhammad, they said: narrated Abdur-Rahman ibn Uthman, Ibrahim ibn Abi Al-Abbas said: son of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Hatib, he said: narrated my father, from his grandfather Muhammad ibn Hatib, from his mother Umm Jamil bint Al-Mujallil, she said: I came with you from the land of Abyssinia until when I was a night or two nights from Madinah, I cooked food for you, then the firewood ran out, so I went out seeking it, then you took hold of the pot and it overturned on your arm, so I brought you to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah, this is Muhammad ibn Hatib. So he spat in your mouth and wiped over your head and supplicated for you, and he kept spitting on your hand and saying: Remove the harm, Lord of the people, and heal, and You are the Healer, there is no healing but Your healing, a healing that leaves no sickness. She said: I did not leave with you from him until your hand healed."
